The amendment commit 7fcff393 answers the r1 findings. No CONTEST item came to this round.

## Paraphrase

### What this track proposes

The addendum makes one app package for each of weeks 2 to 7. It runs the Phase 7 book-picture script on 6 weeks and writes 108 JPEGs and 6 provenance files. It writes 18 image.file lines into each week file. A separate commit after the picture content sets approval.images of each week from the owner answer of 2026-11-05. The match step of the script changes to the positional rule E9. Three test cases go into the existing book-pictures test file, and the loops-content compare drops image.file. It sends 6 hand-off folders to the PM by 2026-11-16 and keeps the other owner items on the 11-16 list.

### How the current system works, per this spec

Weeks 2 to 7 are draft packages. Their text and Thai approvals are approved; the images, audio, song, scripts and loops approvals are draft. No book cover or page of these weeks names a picture, so the app route answers 404. The Phase 7 script matches pictures.json rows by week, use and text, requires exactly one row for each book picture, resolves the COLOR file through the Forge manifest, writes 1600 px JPEGs and one provenance file, and adds image.file lines. Week 1 is published, its 18 pictures are set, and the book-pictures check reads them.

## Findings

- F1 [Blocker] Addendum Overview and FR 1: closed by the amendment. E9 gives the rule for a repeated page text, and the Overview no longer claims the script works for any week without a change.
- F2 [Major] FR 6 and E7: closed. E7 names dashboard/__tests__/storytime-book-pictures.test.ts, the three cases, their week, and their assertions.
- F3 [Major] E5 and E3: closed. E3 sets the approval order, and E5 names the commit that the folder takes.
- F4 [Nit] Blast radius: closed. The blast radius gives the grep, the two whole-week tests and a changes or no change list.
- F5 [Major] E7 case (c) and AC3: the sentence "The case (c) passes before the change" is false, and AC3 names only the cases (a) and (b) as the new assertions. Rationale: remove the row l2-w02-story-page-nan-can-b and the current script finds exactly one candidate for "Nan can.", gives that row to page 1 and page 4, and exits 0 (set-book-pictures.ts line 51 filters the rows and line 52 tests the count; resolveStorytimePictureFiles returns one file for each requested row, picture-check.ts line 616); the case (c) assertion fails before the change and passes only after the count rule of E9 line 144; the Red gate then shows 3 failing cases, not the 2 that AC3 names.
- F6 [Nit] E7 and FR 6 (also the plan blast radius): the rule "No test writes into content/storytime/" is not true for the whole test file. Rationale: storytime-book-pictures.test.ts lines 99 to 101 run main on the shipped w01, and set-book-pictures.ts lines 111 to 117 write the 18 JPEGs and pictures.sha256 with the same bytes; a maker who reads the rule as absolute can remove the only CLI test; write "no new case writes" instead.
- F7 [Nit] Blast radius (also the plan blast radius): "the two tests that read every week" is a wrong count. Rationale: at least ten test files read all eight shipped weeks (for example storytime-print-weeks-2-8.test.ts line 21, storytime-print-d4-prompt.test.ts line 21, storytime-print-v15.test.ts line 35); the phase-end PROJECT_TESTS catches a break, so the risk is low; the wording can make the maker skip a test.

## Withdrawals with evidence

1. F1 withdrawn: E9 lines 140 to 145 give the positional rule. set-book-pictures.ts lines 50 to 54 hold the match step. readers.ts lines 142 to 153 hold rowsByBook. pictures.ts lines 215 to 218 emit each book's pages in order and then its cover, so file order equals page order. pictures.json lines 586, 600, 614, 628, 642, 656, 2276 and 2322 hold the stated ids. The w02 decodable pages 1 to 6 and the w06 decodable pages 3 and 6 hold the stated texts. The stems are 2-can-i and 2-tap-tap.
2. F2 withdrawn: E7 names the file and the cases. Plan lines 115 and 116 add the file to the gates. The existing test lines 76 to 97 run setBookPictures on temp folders with a rowsFile.
3. F3 withdrawn: E3 sets the order of the commits. E5 names the folder commit and forbids a second folder. Plan lines 127, 129 and 130 match.
4. F4 withdrawn: the blast radius gives the grep, the two tests (line 443 and line 264) and the list duty.

## Zero-decision check

The plan names the schema (no change), the CLI (no change), the dependency (sharp), the edge cases (E9, the count rule of line 144, w01 byte-equal) and every file. One gap stays in the test plan: F5.

## Zoom-out check

The addendum solves the root problem (the app has no pictures for weeks 2 to 7). It adds no speculative feature and no premature optimization. It reuses set-book-pictures.ts, checkBookPictures and resolveStorytimePictureFiles. It puts the work in the Phase 7 place. It stays at the requirement level.

